course: dictionary
lesson: 4535
title: Heard: sound, news and knowing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word heard is the past of hear. It can mean you noticed a sound with your ears, or that you were told some news. The words around it show which meaning it has. «I heard a bang» means your ears picked up a noise a moment ago.
explain: Heard can also mean you were told something by someone else: «I heard that school is closed.» You learned the news from somebody. Before you believe a rumour, ask who told it, and whether anyone else says the same.
explain: Heard of is different. It means you know that something exists: «Have you heard of this game?» This does not mean you heard a sound. It means you know about the game.
explain: In a story, «heard footsteps» is a clue. A character noticed a sound, and the reader starts to wonder who is coming. Read the sentences around heard to find the clue.
fact: Heard is the past of hear: hear, hears, heard, heard, hearing.
fact: «Heard» can mean you noticed a sound with your ears, as in «I heard a bang».
fact: «Heard» can mean you were told news, as in «I heard that school is closed».
fact: «Heard of» means you know that something exists.
fact: Other phrases: heard about, heard from, never heard of, overheard.
exercise: «I heard a bang in the kitchen.» What does heard mean here? | You forgot the answer | You touched something hard | *You noticed a sound with your ears
exercise: Mia says, «I heard that school is closed tomorrow.» What does heard mean here? | You made a loud noise | *You were told the news | You looked at the sky
exercise: «Have you heard of this game?» What does heard of mean? | You have lost the game | You have played the game and won | *You know that the game exists
test: «If you heard a smoke alarm, what should you do?» | *Get out of the building safely | Hide under the bed | Turn up the music | Stay in bed and wait
test: Which sentence uses heard to mean you were told news? | Heard footsteps on the stairs | I heard the thunder last night | *I heard that the park is closed today | We heard the dog barking
exam: Which word is the past of hear? | hear | hears | *heard | hearing
